From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Denis Andreyev <257564291+unsound-mint@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 14:00:00 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] Optional live channel range per pixel (filename_range)

Mosaics of observing blocks give each pixel its own contiguous range of
observed channels, with fill zeros outside it and no data beyond the survey
edge. With filename_range, residuals outside a pixel's range carry no weight
in the data term and its gradient, and a pixel with an empty range has no
data term at all.

Coarse levels take the union of the children's ranges and average each
channel over the children observed in it; the coarse noise is the mean over
children with data. A pixel without data gets the level's largest amplitude
bound, since init_bounds would pin its amplitudes at 0. Off by default: without
the key every change is skipped.
